.TH PRO-UPDATES-GUI 1 "2026-10-09" "pro-updates 1.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pro-updates-gui \- the Pro Updates window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pro-updates-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
A GTK window with the same sections as
.BR pro-updates (1),
plus the transport policy (https only, or http allowed for a local mirror),
when the package lists were last downloaded, which repository each browser,
mail client and editor would update from, and builds from source described by
build.json files.
.PP
Changes are made only when you press a button. Root work goes through
.I /usr/libexec/pro-updates/pro-updates-helper
started with pkexec, which shows the polkit message of
.I io.github.defcom5-rockchip.pro-updates.helper
and asks for the password each time. apt never removes a package from the
window. A system-wide Flatpak update follows Flatpak's own polkit rules
(by default no password for updating apps that are already installed).
The helper's apt output is also written to
.IR /var/log/pro-updates.log .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PROUPDATES_BUILD_DIRS
Extra folders to search for build.json files, colon-separated.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pro-updates (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
